    description: "- **Subject:** Two spec sections give mutually inconsistent contracts for the same entrypoint-confidence field.\n- **Mechanic:** One spec section models entrypoint `confidence` as a discrete four-tier value; another spec section models the same field as continuous (penalties of −50%/−70%/−50% plus a connectivity boost up to +0.25). The two sections describe the same field under contradictory contracts.\n- **Expectation:** The two spec sections should be reconciled into one coherent contract for the field.\n- **Scope:** The same `confidence` field is documented as discrete tiers in one section and as a continuous penalty+boost computation in another.\n- **Exposure:** Any reader of the spec trying to determine what the entrypoint confidence value means or how to interpret it.\n- **Consequence:** The reader cannot determine the field's contract — whichever section they trust, the other contradicts it — so any interpretation or reproduction of entrypoint confidence is built on an internally inconsistent spec.\n\n---\n\n(Filed from dogfooding.)"  # 0f78
    fields: {}  # 0f78
