- op: discuss  # ef1d
  at: '2026-07-30T17:47:10Z'  # ef1d
  by: agent  # ef1d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ef1d
  clock: 3  # ef1d
  nonce: ef1d  # ef1d
  message: "DONE — spec-only. The two contradicting descriptions turned out to be describing what are now TWO DIFFERENT FIELDS, so the contradiction dissolves rather than needing a winner.\n\nThe section modelled entrypoint confidence as discrete four-tier in one place and as continuous (penalties of x0.1/x0.3/x0.5 plus a boost) in another. ADR-0039 split those roles: confidence became pure detection reliability holding only the discrete base, and every penalty/demotion/boost moved to rank_score (thread A PR-4, closing WI-lutad + WI-dojor). The spec had NOT been updated — it still said the penalties apply to confidence and that the move was 'slated', a forward-looking phrase describing something already shipped.\n\nVerified on a fresh self-survey: all 118 entrypoints carry BOTH fields; confidence holds the discrete bases while rank_score spans 0.345-1.000 continuously.\n\nFixed en route, same root: SORTING was documented on the wrong key. The spec said 'Ranked by confidence (highest first)'; entrypoints.py:1600 sorts by rank_score, and the emitted array is verifiably ordered by rank_score and NOT by confidence (checked both orderings directly). Two producer docstrings (entrypoints.py:41 and the detect_entrypoints Returns block) repeated the stale claim and were corrected too — leaving them would have let the contradiction be restored from the code side by anyone trusting the docstring over the sort."  # ef1d
